# Vendored subset of 9-cc (https://github.com/0intro/9-cc @ 634e7371,
# "master" as of 2022-04-04), the pieces Harvey needs to build `iar` —
# the Inferno/Plan 9 archiver used as `ar` in the unix build
# (see BUILD_ON_UNIX and build/BUILD_IN_DOCKER).
#
# Layout mirrors upstream, minus everything unrelated to iar:
#   include/    shared headers (a.out.h, ar.h, bio.h, fcall.h, mach.h)
#   cmd/*/      *.out.h object format headers referenced by libmach
#   lib9/       posix subset of src/lib9 (+ linux/ darwin/ per-host lib9.h)
#   libbio/     src/libbio
#   libmach/    src/libmach
#   iar/        src/cmd/iar (ar.c + posix.c)
#
# Local modifications vs upstream:
#   * lib9/getcallerpc.c — single portable version using
#     __builtin_return_address; replaces per-platform asm variants
#     (9-cc ships none for MacOSX-arm/amd64 or Linux-arm64).
#   * lib9/darwin/lib9.h — removed the <architecture/i386/fpu.h> FPU block
#     (x86-only header, gone from modern macOS SDKs).
#   * libmach/vdb.c + vcodas.c — renamed static `fsub` to `vfsub`; glibc >= 2.44 in
#     C23 mode declares fsub() via bits/mathcalls-narrow.h.
#   * libmach arm64 (7-format) support added, from the pinned 9front donor
#     (https://github.com/9front/9front @ 350266104f1fed81c78c3d05fa44f523bec0ae4d,
#     branch "front", pinned 2026-10-31; the same pin as sys/src/cmd/7{a,c,l}):
#       - cmd/7c/7.out.h — donor-verbatim arm64 object format header
#         (same file as sys/src/cmd/7c/7.out.h)
#       - libmach/ureg7.h — donor-verbatim arm64/include/ureg.h (the
#         frozen trap frame; u64int typedefs come from lib9.h)
#       - libmach/7obj.c, libmach/7.c — donor sys/src/libmach copies,
#         byte-identical except the include block adapted to this
#         tree's idiom (<lib9.h> instead of <u.h><libc.h>, quoted
#         "mach.h", "ureg7.h" local include per the ureg6.h pattern)
#       - libmach/obj.c — _is7/_read7 decls + [ObjArm64] "arm64 .7"
#         parser-table row (the enum already existed; the row was
#         missing upstream)
#       - libmach/executable.c — extern marm64 + donor-verbatim
#         R_MAGIC exectab entry + FARM64 commonboot case
#     Motivation: iar writes an archive's __.SYMDEF only when every
#     member parses as a known object; without 7-format support, `ar vu`
#     of .7 objects produced a symdef-less libc.a that 7l cannot link.
#     The same libmach extension also backs the host nm build
#     (sys/src/cmd/nm.BUILD).
#   * BUILD — CFLAGS gains -Wno-error=format-security (the nix devshell
#     cc wrapper injects -Werror=format-security, which errors as
#     "ignored without -Wformat" against this tree's -Wno-format).
#   * libmath/libregexp and the rest of src/cmd are not vendored
#     (iar links only against mach/bio/9).
